# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the litmus compliance suite.
#
# litmus and the neon library it is built on allocate their test state
# and per-request data with the ne_* wrappers without always freeing
# it (for example, the whole PROPFIND request and expat parser graph
# is left behind by the props suite, and neon's lock discovery leaks
# the parsed owner strings).  These are bugs in the third-party test
# suite, not in phodav; until they are fixed upstream, suppress them
# here so that they do not drown out leaks in the phodav code.
#
# The file is only loaded by the litmus test (see meson.build), so
# leaks of the phodav test server running alongside it, which does
# not use neon, are still reported.
leak:ne_malloc
leak:ne_calloc
leak:ne_realloc
leak:ne_strdup
leak:ne_strndup
# neon lock discovery parses the lock owner with plain strdup()
leak:end_element_common
